From 3d880749ff46ba659f7de5ea87ae744214e801eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:38:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: keep no picture where the vblanks cannot pace
 it

A picture of native Dolby Vision output that is on the screen and would be
drawn again the same way is kept there (kodi-9268), and the loop is paced by
the vblanks of the CRTC. nvidia-drm with its defaults has no vblank at all:
its module parameter vblank is off, drm_vblank_init() is not called, and the
ioctl returns EOPNOTSUPP. Every keep then presented nothing, slept 10 ms and
forgot the picture, and the next pass drew it again, late: in a host model of
the loop, 126 of 631 refreshes of a film at 59.94 Hz showed another picture
than the one of their time, against none with every refresh drawn (1.0 RC1).
The commit message of kodi-9268 said that such an output draws every frame;
it did not.

CDVRepeatKeep now remembers it: EOPNOTSUPP for the device until Kodi is
started again, any other failure for the native output in which it happened.
From then on the pictures are drawn again every refresh, as in 1.0 RC1, and
the log says so once.

The line of every 10 s tells how many pictures that were on the screen were
drawn again, and why (keeping turned off, no vblank, drawn over, drawn
another way, the output changing, the flip before not reported).

And, off by default to be measured on a GPU first, video/dvkeepbycommit in
advancedsettings.xml: a kept picture is committed again, as it is, in a
commit that waits for its flip, which paces the loop without any vblank. Only
after a frame presented the way that waits; after a frame presented a frame
ahead the vblanks are still needed. A refused commit turns it off for the
native output. Such a commit counts for CDVPresentStall like any plain frame.
